      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking high-dose vitamin C is actually not recommended for preventing kidney stones because your body converts excess ascorbic acid into oxalate, which can form calcium oxalate stones. Instead, increasing your water intake to about 2–3 liters daily and limiting caffeine and salt are much safer and more effective strategies. Always consult your nephrologist before starting any new supplement regimen, especially one affecting stone composition.",
      "source": "target",
